  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN milky-dark chocolates. The ithi^{th}ith chocolate has a sweetness value of AiA_iAi​, and a bitterness value of BiB_iBi​. Note that both values can be negative.\n\nYou are going to eat all NNN chocolates in a period of KKK days.\n\nOn the first day, you start with the first chocolate. Each subsequent day, you continue eating from where you left off the previous day, consuming a contiguous block of chocolates.\n\nYour mood for that day equals the **minimum** of total sweetness and total bitterness of the chocolates you ate.\n\nYour overall mood equals the sum of moods during the KKK days. Find the **minimum** value of overall mood.\n\nNote that, you must eat **at least** 111 chocolate each day and no chocolate should be left after KKK days.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the number of chocolates and the number of days, respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers, A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the sweetness values of chocolates.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers, B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​ — the bitterness values of chocolates.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **minimum** value of overall mood.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤K≤min⁡(N,300)1 \\leq K \\leq \\min{(N, 300)}1≤K≤min(N,300)",
      "−109≤Ai,Bi≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (60 points):** K≤20K \\leq 20K≤20",
      "**Subtask 2 (40 points):** No further constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n7 3\n-10 8 10 -9 9 -8 -8\n10 -7 9 -10 -4 -5 -3\n2 2\n10 11\n12 13",
        "output": "-38\n21",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: You can eat 111 chocolate on the first day, 444 chocolates on the second day, and 222 chocolates on the third day to finish all NNN chocolates in KKK days.\n\nYour mood for the first day is min⁡(A1,B1)=min⁡(−10,10)=−10\\min(A_1, B_1) = \\min(-10, 10) = -10min(A1​,B1​)=min(−10,10)=−10.\nYour mood for the second day is min⁡(A2+A3+A4+A5,B2+B3+B4+B5)=min⁡(18,−12)=−12\\min(A_2 + A_3 + A_4 + A_5, B_2 + B_3 + B_4 + B_5) = \\min(18, -12) = -12min(A2​+A3​+A4​+A5​,B2​+B3​+B4​+B5​)=min(18,−12)=−12.\nYour mood for the third day is min⁡(A6+A7,B6+B7)=min⁡(−16,−8)=−16\\min(A_6 + A_7, B_6 + B_7) = \\min(-16, -8) = -16min(A6​+A7​,B6​+B7​)=min(−16,−8)=−16.\n\nYour overall mood is (−10)+(−12)+(−16)=−38(-10) + (-12) + (-16) = -38(−10)+(−12)+(−16)=−38, which is minimum possible.\nTest case 222: The only possible way is to eat one chocolate each day.\n\nYour mood for the first day is min⁡(A1,B1)=min⁡(10,12)=10\\min(A_1, B_1) = \\min(10, 12) = 10min(A1​,B1​)=min(10,12)=10\nYour mood for the second day is min⁡(A2,B2)=min⁡(11,13)=11\\min(A_2, B_2) = \\min(11, 13) = 11min(A2​,B2​)=min(11,13)=11\n\nYour overall mood is 10+11=2110+11=2110+11=21."
      }
    ]
  },
